   - The formula for the perimeter of a rectangle is \( P = 2 \times (\text{length} + \text{breadth}) \).
   - Given the length is 27 cm and the breadth is 17 cm, the perimeter is \( P = 2 \times (27 + 17) = 2 \times 44 = 88 \) cm.
2. When the wire is rebent to form a square, the perimeter of the square will be the same as the perimeter of the rectangle.
   - The perimeter of a square is given by \( P = 4 \times \text{side length} \).
   - We already know the perimeter is 88 cm, so we set up the equation \( 4 \times \text{side length} = 88 \).
3. Solve for the side length of the square:
   - Dividing both sides of the equation by 4, we get \( \text{side length} = \frac{88}{4} = 22 \) cm.
Thus, the measure of each side of the square is 22 cm. Therefore, the correct answer is:
C) 22
